id: navigation-bar
name: Navigation bar (bottom, 3 to 5 destinations)
category: navigation
summary: Phone bottom navigation. 80dp tall with a 64x32dp pill that marks the active destination.
requires: foundation
@@spec
- Height 80dp (min-height, so the iOS/Android safe-area inset can add to it, never shrink it).
- 3 to 5 destinations. Each: icon 24dp inside a 64x32dp indicator pill, label below in Label Medium.
- Active: indicator fills with secondary-container, icon fills, label goes bold and on-surface. The indicator grows in with a spatial spring.
- Container: surface-2. Use on compact widths only (under 40rem). Medium widths get a navigation rail, expanded widths a drawer.
- Labels are always visible, never icon-only.
@@a11y
- <nav aria-label="Primary">. Destinations are links, not buttons.
- The active destination carries aria-current="page", not just a class.
- Icons are aria-hidden. The label is the name.
- A badge count needs a text equivalent in the label ("Inbox, 3 unread").
@@html
<nav class="md-nav-bar" aria-label="Primary">
  <a class="md-nav-bar__item" href="/" aria-current="page">
    <span class="md-nav-bar__indicator"><span class="md-icon md-icon--filled" aria-hidden="true">home</span></span>
    <span class="md-nav-bar__label">Home</span>
  </a>
  <a class="md-nav-bar__item" href="/news">
    <span class="md-nav-bar__indicator"><span class="md-icon" aria-hidden="true">newspaper</span></span>
    <span class="md-nav-bar__label">News</span>
  </a>
  <a class="md-nav-bar__item" href="/calendar">
    <span class="md-nav-bar__indicator"><span class="md-icon" aria-hidden="true">calendar_month</span></span>
    <span class="md-nav-bar__label">Calendar</span>
  </a>
</nav>
@@css
.md-nav-bar {
  position: fixed;
  inset-inline: 0;
  bottom: 0;
  z-index: 20;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-around;
  align-items: flex-start;
  min-height: calc(5rem + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0rem));
  padding: var(--sp-md) var(--sp-sm) calc(var(--sp-lg) + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0rem));
  background: var(--md-surface-2);
  color: var(--md-on-surface-variant);
}

.md-nav-bar__item {
  flex: 1;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--sp-xs);
  min-width: 3rem;
  color: inherit;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.md-nav-bar__indicator {
  position: relative;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  width: 4rem;
  height: 2rem;
  border-radius: var(--shape-full);
  isolation: isolate;
}

.md-nav-bar__indicator::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: -1;
  border-radius: var(--shape-full);
  background: var(--md-secondary-container);
  opacity: 0;
  transform: scaleX(0.4);
  transition:
    transform var(--md-spring-fast-spatial-dur) var(--md-spring-fast-spatial),
    opacity var(--md-spring-fast-effects-dur) var(--md-spring-fast-effects);
}

.md-nav-bar__item:hover .md-nav-bar__indicator::before {
  opacity: 1;
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--md-on-surface) 8%, transparent);
  transform: scaleX(1);
}

.md-nav-bar__item[aria-current="page"] { color: var(--md-on-surface); }
.md-nav-bar__item[aria-current="page"] .md-nav-bar__indicator { color: var(--md-on-secondary-container); }
.md-nav-bar__item[aria-current="page"] .md-nav-bar__indicator::before {
  opacity: 1;
  background: var(--md-secondary-container);
  transform: scaleX(1);
}

.md-nav-bar__label {
  font-size: var(--md-type-label-medium-size);
  font-weight: var(--md-type-label-medium-weight);
  line-height: var(--md-type-label-medium-line);
  letter-spacing: var(--md-type-label-medium-tracking);
}
.md-nav-bar__item[aria-current="page"] .md-nav-bar__label { font-weight: 700; }

/* leave room so page content never hides behind the fixed bar */
.md-has-nav-bar { padding-bottom: calc(5rem + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0rem)); }

@media (min-width: 40rem) {
  .md-nav-bar { display: none; }
  .md-has-nav-bar { padding-bottom: 0; }
}
@@notes
Icon names (home, newspaper, calendar_month) must exist in the Material Symbols subset you ship.
